)

# The red control for the GUID itself: the ESP type, which the block-gate disk
# also carries — deliberately, and filled with a byte pattern that is not a
# `.cryostore`. So this configuration locates a partition successfully and then
# REFUSES on the store header, which is a different failure from "no partition
# found" and proves two things one gate could not: that the reader reads at the
# partition it was told about rather than at a fixed place, and that the bytes it
# gets back are the bytes that are there. A run that matched zeros against zeros
# could not tell those apart.
cerise_config_values(
    name = "cryogen_vmm_wrongguid_cvf",
    cm = ":cryogen_vmm_manifest",
    tags = ["manual"],
    values = {
